{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > paper_draft/README.md <<'EOF'\n# Paper draft\n\nOpen \"'`main.pdf` for the compiled manuscript. Edit `main.tex`, the modular files under `sections/` and `appendix/`, and `references.bib` for revisions.\n\nBuild from this directory:\n\n```bash\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode main.tex\nbibtex main\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode main.tex\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode main.tex\n```\n\nThe manuscript follows the supplied experiment report. It does not report new experiments. Tables of extended intervals are transcribed programmatically from `../results/paired_comparisons.csv`. The dose figure is replotted from cached outputs with the original bootstrap convention; regenerate with `../.venv/bin/python figures/plot_dose.py` from this directory. Other result plots are copied from the experiment artifacts. The method diagram is native LaTeX.\n\nThe supplied `neurips_2025.sty` leaves its track-name macro undefined with the requested `[final]` option alone. `commands/macros.tex` defines a manuscript footer so that the exact requested package line compiles without implying conference acceptance.\n\nThe author block is exactly `Ari Holtzman and NeuriCo`. Bibliographic details derive from the supplied literature review and local paper manifest. Undated model cards use `n.d.` with the recorded access date. No example manuscripts were present in `paper_examples/`; its README was the only available file.\n\nThe evidence-mapped outline is `../paper/OUTLINE.md`. `REVIEW.md` records final checks; build logs and PDF page renders are retained for inspection.\nEOF\ncat > paper_draft/REVIEW.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Final manuscript review\n\n- [x] Read paper-writer SKILL.md and complete lab writing guide before drafting.\n- [x] Inspected all supplied command templates; project macros customized.\n- [x] Checked paper_examples/: only README exists, no example manuscripts available.\n- [x] Saved evidence-mapped outline before prose in paper/OUTLINE.md.\n- [x] Used exact requested author and NeurIPS package line, all three command imports, hyperref, booktabs, and plainnat.\n- [x] Abstract is within 150–250 words; all requested sections contain substantive text and section commands.\n- [x] Introduction includes question, motivation, gap, method figure, quantitative preview, three action-led contributions, and organization.\n- [x] Distinguished confirmed primary style contrast from exploratory comparisons; included bootstrap intervals, Holm correction, effect sizes, and quality margins.\n- [x] Preserved null/disagreement findings and separated readout transfer from causal transfer.\n- [x] Distinguished coherence damage from inconclusive coverage noninferiority; no unsupported claim of preserved content or Assistant Axis separation.\n- [x] Explained matching, seeds, intervention position/norm, nuisance estimation, calibration limitations, source grouping, and inference assumptions.\n- [x] Tables use booktabs without vertical rules; AUROC table bolds numerical row maxima with an explicit caveat. Intervention tradeoffs are not assigned a misleading overall winner.\n- [x] Figures and tables have self-contained captions. Replotted dose panels in a larger 2-by-2 layout for readability.\n- [x] Checked primary values and full condition intervals against cached results, and reliability/filter definitions against artifacts/code.\n- [x] Included all ten literature-review papers plus checkpoint/detector/catalog resources in BibTeX.\n- [x] Compiled with pdflatex, bibtex, pdflatex, pdflatex; final logs contain no errors, unresolved references/citations, overfull boxes, or BibTeX warnings.\n- [x] Rendered and visually inspected PDF pages, including title, main results, figures, appendix tables, and references. Verified PDF links and absence of unresolved question marks or replacement glyphs.\n\nScope: paper generation and cached-artifact verification only; experimental model inference was not rerun. No claim is made that the manuscript is accepted at NeurIPS or that model-card publication dates are known.\nEOF\n.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport pymupdf as fitz\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=fitz.open('paper_draft/main.pdf')\nfor i,page in enumerate(p):page.get_pixmap().save(f'paper_draft/review/page-{i+1:02}.png')\nPath('paper_draft/review/extracted.txt').write_text('\\\\n'.join(x.get_text() for x in p))\nprint('Final PDF:',len(p),'pages;',sum(len(x.get_links()) for x in p),'links')\nprint('Last pages:',[(i+1,len(p[i].get_text())) for i in range(max(0,len(p)-4),len(p))])\nlog=Path('paper_draft/build-pass3.log').read_text()\nassert not any(x in log for x in ['Undefined control sequence','LaTeX Warning','Overfull','\"'! LaTeX Error'\"','Package natbib Warning'])\nassert 'Warning' not in Path('paper_draft/build-bibtex.log').read_text()\nprint('Final compilation checks passed')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
